  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.240.90:\n\t\t- Fixed: several responses carried fields this client did not model, which fails the WHOLE\n\t\t  response in a Debug build because MissingMemberHandling.Error is set there. Release builds\n\t\t  ignore unmodelled members and were unaffected, so this restores the ability to test rather\n\t\t  than changing runtime behaviour. Found by sweeping live portal responses against the\n\t\t  models, endpoint by endpoint, rather than one failure at a time.\n\t\t- Reports: AlertsReport gains isEscalation, isIncludeDeletedResourceOrWebsite, logPartition\n\t\t  and suppressionType. ServerCpuReport, ResourceInventoryReport, ResourceMetricTrendsReport,\n\t\t  InterfaceBandwidthReport and SlaReport gain propertyFilterMetric, modelled by the new\n\t\t  PropertyFilterMetric type. ResourceGroupInventoryReport and InterfaceBandwidthReport gain\n\t\t  columns.\n\t\t- Dashboards: AlertWidgetFilter and ParsedAlertFilters gain suppressionType and\n\t\t  isIncludeDeletedResourceOrWebsite; a widget carries both under filters and parsedFilters,\n\t\t  so both types needed them. NocWidget gains displayClearedAlert.\n\t\t- ResourceGroup gains tenantIdentifier, the same field Role gained in 3.240.88.\n\t\t- Collector gains archType, cpAgent, logCollectorGroupId and logCollectorGroupName.\n\t\t- Swept and found complete, so unchanged: Alert, Resource, ScheduledDownTime, and all\n\t\t  twenty widget types other than NocWidget. LogicModules and netscans were not swept.\n\t\t  Websites were not either, and will not be: LogicMonitor has retired them for new portals,\n\t\t  where the same things appear as services or resources instead.",
